# Ignore everything by default...
/*

# ...except top-level source/doc files.
!/*.py
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/CLAUDE.md
!/.gitignore
!/requirements.txt

# ...and the systemd unit files.
!/systemd/
!/systemd/*.service

# ...and tempWork/ scripts -- runtime state (logs, status files) stays
# ignored, only the code is tracked. See root CLAUDE.md's "tempWork"
# section: this whole directory is meant to be short-lived, archived or
# deleted once whatever it exists for resolves. Same two-step pattern as
# projects/ below: unignore the directory for traversal, re-deny
# everything inside, then selectively re-allow just *.py.
!/tempWork/
/tempWork/**
!/tempWork/*.py

# ...and utils/ -- reusable, not-project-specific scripts/notes saved
# over time (see utils/README.md).
!/utils/
/utils/**
!/utils/*.py
!/utils/*.md

# ...and the projects/ tree, but ONLY CLAUDE.md files at any depth --
# everything else under projects/ is real project content, mirrored to
# Google Drive by drive_sync.py instead of living in git (see root
# CLAUDE.md's Projects section). Directories need traversal explicitly
# allowed even though their other files stay ignored, hence the
# trailing-slash line.
!/projects/
/projects/**
!/projects/**/
!/projects/**/CLAUDE.md

/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime/ephemeral state -- deliberately NOT backed up via git, unlike
# bayhouse's own tracked .db files. queue.db is a transient work queue
# (a processed message has no lasting value); logs.db/logs/ are
# regenerated by logging_server.py. The durable record is CLAUDE.md's
# own checkpoint commits, not this.
/queue.db
/queue.db-wal
/queue.db-shm
/logs.db
/logs/

# venv, credentials -- never committed.
/venv/
